this is a python calulator that uses ohms law too calculate voltage, current , ressitance, and electrical power.
it allows users to select a calculation from a menu and enter required values.
the calculator also includes input validtion and a warning for high power calculations.
how to run the python
1. make sure python is installed on your computer.
2. open the project folder in vs code.
3. open the terminal in vs code.
run the following commandthis is a python calulator that uses ohms law too calculate voltage, current , ressitance, and electrical power.
it allows users to select a calculation from a menu and enter required values.
the calculator also includes input validtion and a warning for high power calculations.
how to run the python
1. make sure python is installed on your computer.
2. open the project folder in vs code.
3. open the terminal in vs code.
run the following command
python ohms_law.py
Sample Output
Welcome to the Ohm’s Law and Power Calculator

1. Calculate voltage
2. Calculate current
3. Calculate resistance
4. Calculate power
5. Exit

Enter your choice: 4
Enter voltage: 20
Enter current: 10
Warning: High power detected!
Calculated power: 200.0 watts
Features

• Calculates voltage using Ohm’s Law.
• Calculates current.
• Calculates resistance.
• Calculates electrical power.
• Handles invalid numerical inputs.
• Displays a warning when calculated power exceeds 100 watts.
• Uses a menu-driven interface.
python ohms_law.py
